FG-021 (approved by orch for the owner 2026-10-25): password-protected OOXML export writes
ECMA-376 Agile encryption (EncryptionInfo 4.4: AES-256, SHA-512, 100000 spins, data
integrity HMAC), the Office 2010+ default, instead of Standard (3.2: AES-128, SHA-1).

StrongEncryptionDataSpace is the only registered com.sun.star.comp.oox.crypto service. It
starts with a Standard2007Engine and switches engine only on import (readEncryptionInfo).
AgileEngine's export path (setupEncryption, writeEncryptionInfo, encrypt) is complete and
unused; this selects it when an export sets up encryption. Import is unaffected.
#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__ (native builds keep upstream's Standard default).

--- a/oox/source/crypto/StrongEncryptionDataSpace.cxx
+++ b/oox/source/crypto/StrongEncryptionDataSpace.cxx
@@ -112,6 +112,14 @@
 
 sal_Bool StrongEncryptionDataSpace::setupEncryption(const Sequence<NamedValue>& rMediaEncData)
 {
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+    // FG-021: write ECMA-376 Agile encryption (AES-256, SHA-512; Office 2010 and later)
+    // instead of Standard (AES-128, SHA-1). AgileEngine has a complete encryption path
+    // (setupEncryption, writeEncryptionInfo, encrypt with data integrity); only this
+    // export entry point never chose it. Import is unaffected: readEncryptionInfo picks
+    // the engine from the file being read.
+    mCryptoEngine.reset(new AgileEngine());
+#endif
     if (!mCryptoEngine)
         return false;
 
